{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/283036-what-type-of-bygones-have-you-made","id":283036,"title":"What type of Bygones have you made?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-15T18:55:12-07:00","id":283036,"title":"What type of Bygones have you made?","content":"What types of Bygones have you created for your games? I am not talking about the kind that have appeared in the Bestiary book but ones either invented by your own imagination or from research that you have made into world myths. Honestly, I think some of my favorite potential candidates are already canonically Fae, such as Satyrs and Brownies and Sidhe, so I have never really been given to creating Bygones. Does anyone have a Lovecraftian horror or old fable given stats that they would like to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T20:40:28-07:00","id":283191,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I like the Bygone Bestiary as a resource since it gives you systems to write up some really odd ideas.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In one game, to surprise/annoy the players, they encountered a Transformer in a story. The characters didn\u2019t know what to make of it and the players were split on what they thought about it, which was kind of fun. He was a small(ish) Drone Aircraft-type vehicle with spying capabilities that turned into a Crinos sized humanoid.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I\u2019ve also used it to write up a half-titan (Greek mythos), and a Coatl that served as a Sorcerer character\u2019s mentor. Also, one of my players used it to write up a Golem one time to play. Worked out interestingly.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T01:24:28-07:00","id":283626,"title":"","content":"Slenderman, it was great! It really played into the whole does the consensus define reality question of mage. There is also a little known modern d20 book called &quot;the book of unremitting horror&quot; that has quite a few awesome monsters to creep into a chronicle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T08:27:56-07:00","id":283872,"title":"","content":"I used the Alimori- flaming horses that eat the hair of women and give men extreme joint pain. I keep coming back to slavic mythology for Changeling, it's never disappointed me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T02:58:53-08:00","id":362248,"title":"","content":"I used the Bestiary for some help making a Faerie Cat. Eventually it became a Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}